  "body": {
    "id": "lem:factorization",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\), every \\(x\\in\\mathcal X\\), and all real \\(s,t\\), \\(F_x(s,t)=\\widehat f_x(s+t)\\phi_1(s)\\phi_2(t)\\) and \\(G_x(s,t)=\\widehat q_x(s+t)\\phi_1(s)\\phi_2(t)\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal X\\)",
      "\\(F_x\\)",
      "\\(G_x\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat f_x\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat q_x\\)",
      "\\(\\phi_1\\)",
      "\\(\\phi_2\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:observable-channels",
      "ass:strata",
      "ass:consistency",
      "ass:error-latent-independence",
      "ass:error-coordinate-independence",
      "ass:compact-dose",
      "ass:bounded-outcome"
    ],
    "justification": "This is the observable two-channel factorization on which injectivity and inference rest.",
    "gap": "Capitao-Miniconi, Gassiat, and Lehéricy analyze only the first identity; the marked identity is absent from their model.",
    "consumer": "The empirical characteristic-function confidence set uses these residual equations jointly.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\), \\(x\\in\\mathcal X\\), and \\(s,t\\in\\mathbb R\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}strata}\\), which is a member condition of \\(\\mathrm{def{:}model\\text{-}class}\\), \\(p_x>0\\), so the conditional channels are defined.  From the definitions of the replicates,\n\\[\n e^{i(sS_1+tS_2)}=e^{i(s+t)A}e^{isU_1}e^{itU_2}.\n\\]\nThe joint independence in \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}error\\text{-}latent\\text{-}independence}\\) and the coordinate independence in \\(\\mathrm{ass{:}error\\text{-}coordinate\\text{-}independence}\\) therefore give\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nF_x(s,t)\n&=E_P[e^{i(s+t)A}\\mid X=x]E_P[e^{isU_1}]E_P[e^{itU_2}]\\\\\n&=\\left\\{\\int_{\\mathcal A}e^{i(s+t)a}f_x(a)\\,da\\right\\}\\phi_1(s)\\phi_2(t)\\\\\n&=\\widehat f_x(s+t)\\phi_1(s)\\phi_2(t).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe same two independence assumptions allow the bounded mark to remain with the latent variables.  Thus, using the definitions of \\(m_x\\) and \\(q_x\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nG_x(s,t)\n&=E_P[Ye^{i(s+t)A}\\mid X=x]E_P[e^{isU_1}]E_P[e^{itU_2}]\\\\\n&=\\left\\{\\int_{\\mathcal A}e^{i(s+t)a}E_P[Y\\mid A=a,X=x]f_x(a)\\,da\\right\\}\\phi_1(s)\\phi_2(t)\\\\\n&=\\widehat q_x(s+t)\\phi_1(s)\\phi_2(t).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nAll expectations are finite: the probability-channel integrands have modulus one, while \\(|Y|\\le B_Y\\) follows from consistency and bounded potential outcomes, both member conditions of \\(\\mathcal M\\).  This proves both identities.",
